@prefix sx: <https://semblance.dev/ns/sparql#> .
@prefix sem: <https://semblance.dev/ns/core#> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .
@prefix beh: <https://semblance.dev/ns/behaviour#> .
@prefix mod: <https://semblance.dev/ns/modality#> .
@prefix sty: <https://semblance.dev/ns/style#> .
@prefix val: <https://semblance.dev/ns/validation#> .
@prefix l10n: <https://semblance.dev/ns/l10n#> .
@prefix key: <https://semblance.dev/ns/keyboard#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Typeaheads: a text field that finds values among options from the graph (DESIGN.md §3, Inputs).
#
#   c:Combobox  sets a single-valued property: c:property of the node it c:controls, like c:Choice.
#   c:TagInput  edits a multi-valued one: its values are removable c:Tag pills before the field.
#
# Where the options come from is said on the instance: an explicit c:options list; else the
# instances of c:optionClass (by default, when there is no c:optionsFrom, the property's
# rdfs:range, as for c:Choice), together with what the node c:optionsFrom names lists (c:lists:
# a c:TermTree lists every term it shows) and, when c:optionsInUse is true, every value the
# property already has on any node. An option is called by its label (c:optionNames c:Labels, the
# default) or by its prefixed name, its label then being a second name it is found by
# (c:PrefixedNames: "c:List", "key:Layer · keyboard"). With
# c:allowsCustom true, text that names no option can be committed as a new value: a literal or a
# new resource with that rdfs:label (c:customAs; by default a literal for an owl:DatatypeProperty,
# a resource otherwise, minted under c:mintBase). What a new value may be, and how many values a
# tag input holds, are SHACL: the validation layer checks the typed text against the
# val:validates shape's value constraints and the controlled values against its sh:minCount /
# sh:maxCount.
#
# Everything is graph state: the typed text (c:value), where the caret is and whether the field
# should hold the focus (c:caret), whether the list is open (c:expanded) and the highlighted
# option (c:activeOption). The WAI-ARIA combobox pattern: the field is role=combobox with
# aria-expanded, aria-controls (the role=listbox popup) and aria-activedescendant (the active
# option), so focus stays in the field while the arrow keys move through the list.
#
# Thousands of options. With c:optionLimit n, the list is only the n best matches of what is typed,
# built while the list is open: an exact name first, then a name or a word of it that starts with
# the text, then any other that contains it, the shorter first (c:TypeaheadMatches, one query per
# keystroke; c:TypeaheadOptions is not run). c:picksFirstMatch true lets Enter take the best match
# when nothing is highlighted, as a search field does.
#
# How a keystroke stays cheap. Typing writes c:value; a function rule folds it (case and
# diacritics, which SPARQL cannot) into c:foldedQuery; then
#   - each option is its own component (c:TypeaheadOption, minted once by c:TypeaheadOptions, or
#     under c:optionLimit only the best few, minted anew by c:TypeaheadMatches as the text changes) whose
#     SPARQL rule decides whether it matches and highlights the matched part: the options are
#     evaluated member-wise, in one bulk query, and only those whose state changed write anything;
#   - the typeahead's own rule (the field, the popup, the "create" and status rows) is O(1) but for
#     two EXISTS over the options' search keys;
#   - the list of options (c:TypeaheadOptions), the pills (c:TagInputPills) and the texts
#     (c:TypeaheadTexts) do not hear about typing at all.
# Moving the active option touches the typeahead's rule only (it writes aria-selected on the
# active option and aria-activedescendant on the field).
#
# Options follow what the typeahead itself does (a value it creates is an option at once) and any
# change to the node it controls. Instances of the option class added elsewhere join the list at
# the next such change, as for c:Choice: SPARQL rules hear their focus and the nodes they follow,
# and a function rule what it read, not every new member of a class. Options a node lists
# (c:optionsFrom) follow its c:lists, and only them: a pick costs what the values changed, however
# many options there are.

<https://semblance.dev/ns/component/typeahead> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Semblance typeaheads: combobox and tag input"@en .

# --- vocabulary ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

c:Typeahead a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf sem:Component ;
    rdfs:comment """A text field with a list of options that typing filters (case- and diacritic-insensitively,
the matched part highlighted). The typed text is c:value, folded into c:foldedQuery; the options are
c:TypeaheadOption components; the highlighted one is c:activeOption. A c:CommandPalette is one whose
options are things to run (palette.ttl); the rest of this comment is about the typeaheads that edit a
property: c:Combobox and c:TagInput. Such a typeahead edits c:property of the node it c:controls. Options: c:options, or the
instances of c:optionClass (default: the property's rdfs:range), plus what a node lists (c:optionsFrom)
and the values in use (c:optionsInUse), called by label or by prefixed name (c:optionNames). For
thousands of options, c:optionLimit lists only the best matches. c:allowsCustom lets text that matches
no option be committed as a new value (c:customAs, c:mintBase). Also: c:label, c:placeholder, c:help,
c:disabled, val:validates, c:picksFirstMatch, and a key:shortcut that focuses the field.
Down and Up move through the shown options (opening the list), Enter picks the highlighted one (or the
one the text names exactly, or creates it, or the only one shown), Escape closes the list and gives the typed text back, and
a second Escape clears it."""@en ;
    sem:slug "typeahead" ;
    c:labelPart "input" .

c:Combobox a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c:Typeahead ;
    rdfs:comment """A typeahead that sets a single-valued property (c:property of c:controls), like a c:Choice you
can type into. The field shows the chosen option's label; typing searches, picking replaces the
value, leaving the field without picking gives the chosen label back."""@en ;
    sem:slug "combobox" ;
    c:labelPart "input" .

c:TagInput a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c:Typeahead ;
    rdfs:comment """A typeahead that edits a multi-valued property: its values are removable c:Tag pills (✕, or
Backspace in the empty field removes the last), and picking an option adds it. With c:allowsCustom,
Enter or a comma adds the typed text as a new value. A value is never added twice, and a sh:maxCount
in the val:validates shape caps how many there are (its sh:message is shown at the cap)."""@en ;
    sem:slug "tag-input" ;
    c:labelPart "input" .

c:optionClass a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ; rdfs:range owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Options from"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Options are the instances of this class (default, without c:optionsFrom: the controlled property's rdfs:range)."@en .
c:optionsFrom a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ;
    rdfs:label "Options listed by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Options are what this node lists (c:lists): a c:TermTree's terms, say. They follow its c:lists exactly."@en .
c:lists a rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:comment "What a node lists, one value each: stated, or derived by a component from what it shows (a c:TermTree lists every term of its sections). A typeahead's c:optionsFrom offers them."@en .
c:optionNames a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ; rdfs:range c:OptionNaming ;
    rdfs:comment "How options are called (default c:Labels)."@en .
c:OptionNaming a owl:Class ; rdfs:comment "How a typeahead calls its options and values."@en .
c:Labels a c:OptionNaming ; rdfs:label "by label"@en ; sem:order 1 ;
    rdfs:comment "By c:label or rdfs:label in the viewer's language, else the IRI's local name; a literal is its own text."@en .
c:PrefixedNames a c:OptionNaming ; rdfs:label "by prefixed name"@en ; sem:order 2 ;
    rdfs:comment "By prefixed name (c:List; sh:prefix declarations), with the label, when it says more, shown after it and searched too (c:detail). A term of an undeclared namespace is called by its label."@en .
c:optionLimit a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ; rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ;
    rdfs:label "Options shown"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "At most this many options are listed: the best matches of the typed text (up to 50, the SPARQL rule's bound), built only while the list is open. For thousands of options."@en .
c:picksFirstMatch a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "true: Enter with typed text and nothing highlighted picks the first option shown (the best match), when no option is named exactly."@en .
c:optionsInUse a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "Options include every value the controlled property already has, on any node (literals too)."@en .
c:allowsCustom a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "Custom values"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Text that matches no option can be committed as a new value (default false: only options can be picked)."@en .
c:customAs a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ; rdfs:range c:CustomValueKind ;
    rdfs:comment "What committing new text makes: a literal or a new resource (default: a literal for an owl:DatatypeProperty, else a resource)."@en .
c:CustomValueKind a owl:Class ; rdfs:comment "What a typeahead makes of text that names no option."@en .
c:NewLiteral a c:CustomValueKind ; rdfs:label "a literal"@en ; sem:order 1 ;
    rdfs:comment "The text itself, as a plain literal."@en .
c:NewResource a c:CustomValueKind ; rdfs:label "a new resource"@en ; sem:order 2 ;
    rdfs:comment "A resource minted under c:mintBase (default: the option class's IRI and \"/\"), typed with the option class, with the text as its rdfs:label."@en .
c:mintBase a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ;
    rdfs:comment "The IRI prefix new resources are minted under: the text, lower-cased with spaces as dashes, is appended."@en .

# State (c:value, the typed text, is shared with the other inputs; c:expanded with disclosures).
c:activeOption a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ;
    rdfs:comment "The highlighted option (an IRI or a literal: the value picking it commits; in a command palette, the c:TypeaheadOption itself). None: nothing is highlighted (a palette then highlights its first shown option)."@en .
# c:caret (workbench.ttl) is where the caret is; on a typeahead its presence also means the field
# keeps the focus after an event (picking, removing a pill), and leaving the field removes it.

# Derived.
c:foldedQuery a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Typeahead ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived: the typed text, trimmed, lower-cased and without diacritics, which the options are matched against."@en .
c:searchKey a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived: a label folded like c:foldedQuery, one character for each of the label's, so that a match's position in it is its position in the label."@en .
c:detail a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived, on a text node and an option: a second name the option is found by and shown with (its label, under c:PrefixedNames)."@en .
c:matchKey a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived: what typing is matched against: the c:searchKey, then, with a c:detail, a line break and the detail folded the same way (a match before the break is in the name, one after it in the detail)."@en .
c:textOf a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range c:Typeahead ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived, on a node minted <typeahead>/~term-<term>: the typeahead whose option or value it describes."@en .
c:textFor a rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived: the option or value (an IRI or a literal) a text node describes (its l10n:label and c:searchKey)."@en .
c:offered a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ; rdfs:comment "Derived, on a text node: the term is one of the options."@en .
c:chosen a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ; rdfs:comment "Derived, on a text node: the term is a current value of the controlled property."@en .
c:rank a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived: where an option sorts (its list position or sem:order, zero-padded, then its search key; under c:optionLimit, how well it matches first), or a pill (its search key). Also its sem:orderKey. A text node of an option has its unlimited rank."@en .
c:option a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain c:TypeaheadOption ; rdfs:comment "The option (an IRI or a literal) a c:TypeaheadOption shows."@en .

# On rendered rows of the list, for the reactions: which typeahead a row belongs to, what picking it
# commits, and (the "create" row) what it would make.
c:optionRow a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range c:Typeahead ;
    rdfs:comment "On a rendered row of a typeahead's list: the typeahead."@en .
c:pick a rdf:Property ; rdfs:comment "On a rendered row: the value picking it commits (and c:activeOption names while it is highlighted)."@en .
c:creates a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:comment "On the rendered \"create\" row: the text it commits (trimmed)."@en .
c:mints a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:comment "On the rendered \"create\" row: the new resource committing it mints (it is also the row's c:pick)."@en .
c:mintClass a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:comment "On the rendered \"create\" row: the class the minted resource is typed with."@en .
# On a pill (a minted c:Tag): the tag input whose value it shows, and the value. Removing the pill is
# the tag input's to do (c:TagInputRemove), not c:TagRemove's.
c:pillOf a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain c:Tag ; rdfs:range c:TagInput ;
    rdfs:comment "On a c:Tag minted by a c:TagInput: the tag input whose value it shows; its ✕ removes that value."@en .
c:tagValue a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain c:Tag ; rdfs:comment "On a pill: the value of the tag input's property it shows."@en .

c:TypeaheadOption a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf sem:Component ;
    rdfs:comment """One option of a typeahead's list (minted by c:TypeaheadOptions under it): c:of the typeahead,
c:option the value, with its c:label, c:searchKey and c:rank. It renders a role=option row, hidden
while it does not match the typed text, the matched part in a <mark>."""@en ;
    sem:slug "typeahead-option" ;
    key:rendersHint true .

# Phrases, translated like the other c:Phrase individuals. "{}" stands for the typed text.
c:NoMatches a c:Phrase ; rdfs:label "No matches"@en , "Нічого не знайдено"@uk , "Keine Treffer"@de , "لا توجد نتائج"@ar .
c:CreatePhrase a c:Phrase ; rdfs:label "Create “{}”"@en , "Створити «{}»"@uk , "„{}“ anlegen"@de , "إنشاء «{}»"@ar .
c:AlreadyAdded a c:Phrase ; rdfs:label "“{}” is already added"@en , "«{}» уже додано"@uk , "„{}“ ist schon hinzugefügt"@de , "«{}» مضاف بالفعل"@ar .

# --- texts: labels in the viewer's language, and search keys ------------------------------------------
# A function layer, like c:ChoiceTexts: before anything renders, every option and every current
# value gets a node <typeahead>/~term-<term> with its label in the viewer's language (or prefixed
# name, c:optionNames), its search and match keys, a detail if it has one, and (an option) its
# rank; the caption and the phrases get theirs too. Two rules: the options' texts, which hear the
# controlled property only when options of a class or in use may change with it (a value created,
# a new instance), and the values' texts, which do (chosen, c:chosen). So a pick over options a node
# lists rewrites two text nodes, not all of them. The option list and the pills read what they
# derive (sem:readsMinted), so they follow the values without hearing typing.

c:TypeaheadTexts a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:targets c:Typeahead ;
    sem:requires c:controls ;
    sem:stratum -20 ;
    sem:inputOnly true ;
    sem:follows c:controls ;
    sem:functionOnly "awaits sx:Locale (sx:sortKey): it folds labels for matching (NFD, combining marks removed, lower-cased); the labels themselves are picked from the viewer's languages in the graph." ;
    sem:needsExtension sx:Locale .
c:TypeaheadTexts-fn a sem:Rule ; sem:implements c:TypeaheadTexts ; sem:function "typeahead:texts" .

c:TypeaheadValueTexts a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:targets c:Typeahead ;
    sem:requires c:controls ;
    sem:stratum -20 ;
    sem:inputOnly true ;
    sem:follows c:controls ;
    sem:functionOnly "awaits sx:Locale (sx:sortKey): it folds the values' labels as c:TypeaheadTexts folds the options' (NFD, combining marks removed, lower-cased)." ;
    sem:needsExtension sx:Locale .
c:TypeaheadValueTexts-fn a sem:Rule ; sem:implements c:TypeaheadValueTexts ; sem:function "typeahead:values" .

c:TypeaheadQuery a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:targets c:Typeahead ;
    sem:stratum -20 ;
    sem:inputOnly true ;
    sem:watches c:value ;
    sem:functionOnly "awaits sx:Locale (sx:sortKey): it folds the typed text as the labels are folded (NFD, combining marks removed, lower-cased)." ;
    sem:needsExtension sx:Locale .
c:TypeaheadQuery-fn a sem:Rule ; sem:implements c:TypeaheadQuery ; sem:function "typeahead:query" .

# --- the field, the popup and their state ------------------------------------------------------------
# One rule per typeahead. It reads the texts layer's nodes (sem:readsMinted) and the controlled
# node (sem:follows c:controls). Ordering: label, field (pills, input, chevron, the popup under it),
# foot (help, a note, the error).

c:TypeaheadRendering a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:awaitsWork <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/14> ; # its function twin comes with the combobox work
    sem:targets c:Typeahead ;
    sem:requires c:controls ;
    sem:stratum 0 ;
    sem:follows c:controls ;
    sem:readsMinted true .
c:TypeaheadRendering-sparql-screen a sem:Rule ;
    sem:implements c:TypeaheadRendering ;
    sem:modality mod:Screen ;
    sem:construct """
CONSTRUCT {
  ?root a rdfhtml:Div ; sem:renders $this ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?label, ?field, ?foot .
  ?label a rdfhtml:Label ; rdfhtml:for ?inputId ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?labelText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?field .
  ?labelText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?caption .
  ?field a rdfhtml:Div ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-field" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?pills, ?input, ?chevron, ?popup ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?foot .
  ?pills a rdfhtml:Ul ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-pills" ; rdfhtml:attribute ?pillsLabel ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?input .
  ?pillsLabel a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-label" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue ?caption .
  ?input a rdfhtml:Input ; rdfhtml:type "text" ; rdfhtml:id ?inputId ; rdfhtml:value ?shown ; rdfhtml:placeholder ?placeholder ;
         rdfhtml:disabled ?disabled ; rdfhtml:autocomplete "off" ; rdfhtml:spellcheck "false" ;
         rdfhtml:attribute ?roleAttr, ?autoAttr, ?controlsAttr, ?expandedAttr, ?activeAttr, ?describedAttr, ?invalidAttr, ?caretAttr ;
         ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?afterInput .
  ?roleAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "role" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "combobox" .
  ?autoAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-autocomplete" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "list" .
  ?controlsAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-controls" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue ?listId .
  ?expandedAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-expanded" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue ?expandedValue .
  ?activeAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-activedescendant" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue ?activeId .
  ?describedAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-describedby" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue ?describedIds .
  ?invalidAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-invalid" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "true" .
  ?caretAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "data-sem-caret" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue ?caretValue .
  ?chevron a rdfhtml:Span ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-chevron" ; rdfhtml:attribute ?chevronHidden, ?chevronKeep ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?chevronText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?popup .
  ?chevronHidden a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-hidden" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "true" .
  ?chevronKeep a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "data-sem-keep-focus" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "" .
  ?chevronText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data "▾" .
  ?popup a rdfhtml:Div ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-popup" ; rdfhtml:hidden ?popupHidden ; rdfhtml:attribute ?popupKeep ;
         rdfhtml:hasChild ?list, ?status .
  ?popupKeep a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "data-sem-keep-focus" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "" .
  ?list a rdfhtml:Ul ; rdfhtml:id ?listId ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-list" ; rdfhtml:hidden ?listHidden ;
        rdfhtml:attribute ?listRole, ?listLabel ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?create ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?status .
  ?listRole a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "role" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "listbox" .
  ?listLabel a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-label" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue ?caption .
  ?create a rdfhtml:Li ; rdfhtml:id ?createId ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-create" ; rdfhtml:attribute ?createRole ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?createText ;
          sem:orderKey "~" ; c:optionRow $this ; c:pick ?createValue ; c:creates ?entry ; c:mints ?mintedValue ; c:mintClass ?mintClass .
  ?createRole a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "role" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "option" .
  ?createText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?createLine .
  ?status a rdfhtml:Div ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-status" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?statusText .
  ?statusText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?statusLine .
  ?foot a rdfhtml:Div ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-foot" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?help, ?note, ?error .
  ?help a rdfhtml:Div ; rdfhtml:id ?helpId ; rdfhtml:class "sem-help" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?helpText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?afterHelp .
  ?helpText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?helpData .
  ?note a rdfhtml:Div ; rdfhtml:id ?noteId ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-note" ; rdfhtml:attribute ?noteRole ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?noteText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?error .
  ?noteRole a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "role" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "status" .
  ?noteText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?fullMessage .
  ?error a rdfhtml:Div ; rdfhtml:id ?errorId ; rdfhtml:class "sem-error" ; rdfhtml:attribute ?errorRole ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?errorText .
  ?errorRole a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "role" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "alert" .
  ?errorText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?errorData .
  ?activeRow rdfhtml:attribute ?selectedAttr .
  ?selectedAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-selected" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "true" .
  ?chosenRow rdfhtml:attribute ?chosenAttr ; rdfhtml:hidden ?chosenHidden .
  ?chosenAttr a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "data-chosen" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "" .
}
WHERE {
  $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:Typeahead ; c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  BIND(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } AS ?multi)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:allowsCustom ?custom0 FILTER(STR(?custom0) = "true") } AS ?custom)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?disabled0 FILTER(STR(?disabled0) = "true") } AS ?isDisabled)
  BIND(IF(?isDisabled, "", ?none) AS ?disabled)
  BIND(!?isDisabled && EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?expanded0 FILTER(STR(?expanded0) = "true") } AS ?open)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:value ?typed0 }
  BIND(STR(?typed0) AS ?typed)
  BIND(REPLACE(COALESCE(?typed, ""), "^\\\\s+|\\\\s+$", "") AS ?entry0)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?query0 }
  BIND(COALESCE(STR(?query0), "") AS ?q)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:placeholder ?placeholder0 }
  BIND(STR(?placeholder0) AS ?placeholder)
  # The caption: the texts layer's (c:label, else the property's label, in the viewer's language).
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~l10n-caption")) AS ?captionNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?captionNode l10n:label ?caption0 } }
  OPTIONAL { ?caption1At l10n:of $this ; l10n:label ?caption1 }
  OPTIONAL { $this c:label ?caption1 FILTER(isLiteral(?caption1) && lang(?caption1) = "") }
  BIND(STR(COALESCE(?caption0, ?caption1, REPLACE(STR(?property), "^.*[#/]", ""))) AS ?caption)
  # A combobox shows its chosen option's label until something is typed.
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?target ?property ?current FILTER(!?multi) } }
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~term-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(COALESCE(?current, ""))))) AS ?currentNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?currentNode l10n:label ?currentLabel0 } }
  BIND(COALESCE(?currentLabel0, IF(isLiteral(?current), STR(?current), REPLACE(STR(?current), "^.*[#/]", ""))) AS ?currentLabel)
  # The highlighted option, while the list is open: the field shows its label.
  OPTIONAL { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
  BIND(IF(?open, ?active0, ?none) AS ?active)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~term-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(COALESCE(?active, ""))))) AS ?activeNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?activeNode l10n:label ?activeLabel } }
  # Phrases in the viewer's language (the texts layer), else English.
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~l10n-no-matches")) AS ?noMatchesNode)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~l10n-create")) AS ?createNode)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~l10n-already-added")) AS ?addedNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?noMatchesNode l10n:label ?noMatches0 } OPTIONAL { ?createNode l10n:label ?createPhrase0 } OPTIONAL { ?addedNode l10n:label ?addedPhrase0 } }
  OPTIONAL { ?noMatches1At l10n:of c:NoMatches ; l10n:name ?noMatches1 }
  OPTIONAL { ?noMatches1At l10n:of c:NoMatches ; l10n:name ?noMatches1 }
  OPTIONAL { c:NoMatches rdfs:label ?noMatches1 FILTER(langMatches(lang(?noMatches1), "en")) }
  OPTIONAL { ?createPhrase1At l10n:of c:CreatePhrase ; l10n:name ?createPhrase1 }
  OPTIONAL { ?createPhrase1At l10n:of c:CreatePhrase ; l10n:name ?createPhrase1 }
  OPTIONAL { c:CreatePhrase rdfs:label ?createPhrase1 FILTER(langMatches(lang(?createPhrase1), "en")) }
  OPTIONAL { ?addedPhrase1At l10n:of c:AlreadyAdded ; l10n:name ?addedPhrase1 }
  OPTIONAL { ?addedPhrase1At l10n:of c:AlreadyAdded ; l10n:name ?addedPhrase1 }
  OPTIONAL { c:AlreadyAdded rdfs:label ?addedPhrase1 FILTER(langMatches(lang(?addedPhrase1), "en")) }
  BIND(STR(COALESCE(?noMatches0, ?noMatches1)) AS ?noMatchesPhrase)
  BIND(STR(COALESCE(?createPhrase0, ?createPhrase1)) AS ?createPhrase)
  BIND(STR(COALESCE(?addedPhrase0, ?addedPhrase1)) AS ?addedPhrase)
  # What the typed text names: an option or a value exactly, a value already added, any option shown.
  BIND(?q != "" && EXISTS { ?known c:textOf $this ; c:searchKey ?q } AS ?isKnown)
  BIND(?multi && ?q != "" && EXISTS { ?added c:textOf $this ; c:chosen true ; c:searchKey ?q } AS ?duplicate)
  BIND(EXISTS { ?shownOption c:textOf $this ; c:offered true ; c:matchKey ?shownKey
                FILTER(CONTAINS(?shownKey, ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?shownOption c:chosen true }) } AS ?anyShown)
  # The validation layer: the typed text breaks the shape (val:invalidEntry), the values fill it (val:full).
  OPTIONAL { $this val:invalidEntry ?entryProblem0 }
  BIND(STR(?entryProblem0) AS ?entryProblem)
  BIND(BOUND(?entryProblem) AS ?entryInvalid)
  OPTIONAL { $this val:full ?full0 FILTER(?multi) }
  BIND(STR(?full0) AS ?fullMessage)
  BIND(BOUND(?fullMessage) AS ?full)
  # The "create" row: new text, allowed, valid, not past the maximum. Its value is what committing it makes.
  BIND(?custom && !?isDisabled && ?entry0 != "" && ?q != "" && !?isKnown && !?entryInvalid && !?full AS ?canCreate)
  BIND(IF(?canCreate, ?entry0, ?none) AS ?entry)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:customAs c:NewLiteral } || (NOT EXISTS { $this c:customAs c:NewResource } && EXISTS { ?property a owl:DatatypeProperty }) AS ?asLiteral)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:optionClass ?declaredClass }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?property rdfs:range ?range FILTER(isIRI(?range) && !STRSTARTS(STR(?range), STR(xsd:)) && ?range != rdfs:Literal) } }
  BIND(IF(?asLiteral, ?none, COALESCE(?declaredClass, ?range)) AS ?mintClass0)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:mintBase ?declaredBase }
  BIND(COALESCE(STR(?declaredBase), CONCAT(STR(COALESCE(?mintClass0, ?property)), "/")) AS ?base)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?entry), IF(?asLiteral, ?entry, IRI(CONCAT(?base, ENCODE_FOR_URI(LCASE(REPLACE(?entry, "\\\\s+", "-")))))), ?none) AS ?createValue)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?entry) && !?asLiteral, ?createValue, ?none) AS ?mintedValue)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?mintedValue), ?mintClass0, ?none) AS ?mintClass)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?entry), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~create")), ?none) AS ?create)
  BIND(STR(?create) AS ?createId)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?create), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~create-role")), ?none) AS ?createRole)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?create), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~create-text")), ?none) AS ?createText)
  BIND(CONCAT(STRBEFORE(?createPhrase, "{}"), ?entry, STRAFTER(?createPhrase, "{}")) AS ?createLine)
  # The status row: already added; else why new text cannot be created (the shape's message); else
  # that nothing matches.
  BIND(IF(?duplicate, CONCAT(STRBEFORE(?addedPhrase, "{}"), ?entry0, STRAFTER(?addedPhrase, "{}")),
          IF(?custom && ?entryInvalid && !?isKnown, ?entryProblem,
             IF(?q != "" && !?anyShown && !?canCreate, ?noMatchesPhrase, ?none))) AS ?statusLine)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?statusLine), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~status")), ?none) AS ?status)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?statusLine), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~status-text")), ?none) AS ?statusText)
  # The popup is shown while open, unless there is nothing in it (or a tag input is full).
  BIND(?open && !?full && (?anyShown || ?canCreate || BOUND(?statusLine)) AS ?popupShown)
  BIND(IF(?popupShown, ?none, "") AS ?popupHidden)
  BIND(IF(?full, "", ?none) AS ?listHidden)
  BIND(IF(?popupShown, "true", "false") AS ?expandedValue)
  # The active row: the create row or an option's, which gets aria-selected.
  BIND(BOUND(?active) && BOUND(?createValue) && sameTerm(?active, ?createValue) AS ?activeCreates)
  BIND(IF(?popupShown && BOUND(?active), IF(?activeCreates, ?create, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~opt-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?active)), "/~root"))), ?none) AS ?activeRow)
  BIND(STR(?activeRow) AS ?activeId)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?activeRow), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~active-aria-selected")), ?none) AS ?selectedAttr)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?activeRow), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input-aria-activedescendant")), ?none) AS ?activeAttr)
  # What the field shows, and where its caret goes (only while it keeps the focus: c:caret).
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?activeRow) && !?activeCreates, ?activeLabel, ?none) AS ?shownActive)
  BIND(COALESCE(?shownActive, ?typed, ?currentLabel, "") AS ?shown)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:caret ?caret0 }
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?caret0), STR(IF(BOUND(?shownActive) || !BOUND(?typed), STRLEN(?shown), xsd:integer(?caret0))), ?none) AS ?caretValue)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?caretValue), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input-data-sem-caret")), ?none) AS ?caretAttr)
  # Help, the note at the maximum, the error; the field is described by those there are.
  OPTIONAL { $this c:help ?help0 }
  OPTIONAL { $this c:error ?error0 }
  BIND(STR(?help0) AS ?helpData)
  BIND(STR(?error0) AS ?errorData)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?helpData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~help")), ?none) AS ?help)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?helpData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~help-text")), ?none) AS ?helpText)
  BIND(IF(?full, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~note")), ?none) AS ?note)
  BIND(IF(?full, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~note-role")), ?none) AS ?noteRole)
  BIND(IF(?full, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~note-text")), ?none) AS ?noteText)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?errorData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~error")), ?none) AS ?error)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?errorData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~error-text")), ?none) AS ?errorText)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?errorData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~error-role")), ?none) AS ?errorRole)
  BIND(STR(?help) AS ?helpId)
  BIND(STR(?note) AS ?noteId)
  BIND(STR(?error) AS ?errorId)
  BIND(COALESCE(?note, ?error) AS ?afterHelp)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?help) || BOUND(?note) || BOUND(?error),
          CONCAT(COALESCE(?helpId, ""), IF(BOUND(?help) && (BOUND(?note) || BOUND(?error)), " ", ""),
                 COALESCE(?noteId, ""), IF(BOUND(?note) && BOUND(?error), " ", ""), COALESCE(?errorId, "")), ?none) AS ?describedIds)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?describedIds), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input-aria-describedby")), ?none) AS ?describedAttr)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?errorData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input-aria-invalid")), ?none) AS ?invalidAttr)
  # The parts.
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~root")) AS ?root)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~label")) AS ?label)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~label-text")) AS ?labelText)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~field")) AS ?field)
  BIND(IF(?multi, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~pills")), ?none) AS ?pills)
  BIND(IF(?multi, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~pills-aria-label")), ?none) AS ?pillsLabel)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input")) AS ?input)
  BIND(STR(?input) AS ?inputId)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input-role")) AS ?roleAttr)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input-aria-autocomplete")) AS ?autoAttr)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input-aria-controls")) AS ?controlsAttr)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input-aria-expanded")) AS ?expandedAttr)
  BIND(IF(?multi, ?none, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~chevron"))) AS ?chevron)
  BIND(IF(?multi, ?none, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~chevron-aria-hidden"))) AS ?chevronHidden)
  BIND(IF(?multi, ?none, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~chevron-keep"))) AS ?chevronKeep)
  BIND(IF(?multi, ?none, IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~chevron-text"))) AS ?chevronText)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~popup")) AS ?popup)
  BIND(COALESCE(?chevron, ?popup) AS ?afterInput)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~popup-keep")) AS ?popupKeep)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~list")) AS ?list)
  BIND(STR(?list) AS ?listId)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~list-role")) AS ?listRole)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~list-aria-label")) AS ?listLabel)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~foot")) AS ?foot)
  # The rows of current values: a combobox marks its chosen option, a tag input hides its pills'.
  {
    {} UNION {
      $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property . ?target ?property ?value .
      BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~opt-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?value)), "/~root")) AS ?chosenRow)
      BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~chosen-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?value)))) AS ?chosenAttr)
      BIND(IF(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput }, "", ?none) AS ?chosenHidden)
    }
  }
}""" .

# Text: one line. A combobox: "Assignee: [Ada Lovelace_] ▾"; a tag input: "Labels: ‹bug› ‹docs› [_]".
c:TypeaheadRendering-sparql-text a sem:Rule ;
    sem:implements c:TypeaheadRendering ;
    sem:modality mod:Text ;
    sem:construct """
CONSTRUCT {
  ?root a rdfhtml:Div ; sem:renders $this ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?line .
  ?line a rdfhtml:Div ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?lineText .
  ?lineText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?lineData .
}
WHERE {
  $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:Typeahead ; c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  BIND($this AS ?self)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } AS ?multi)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~l10n-caption")) AS ?captionNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?captionNode l10n:label ?caption0 } }
  OPTIONAL { ?caption1At l10n:of $this ; l10n:label ?caption1 }
  OPTIONAL { $this c:label ?caption1 FILTER(isLiteral(?caption1) && lang(?caption1) = "") }
  BIND(STR(COALESCE(?caption0, ?caption1, REPLACE(STR(?property), "^.*[#/]", ""))) AS ?caption)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:value ?typed0 }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?target ?property ?current FILTER(!?multi) } }
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~term-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(COALESCE(?current, ""))))) AS ?currentNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?currentNode l10n:label ?currentLabel0 } }
  BIND(COALESCE(?currentLabel0, IF(isLiteral(?current), STR(?current), REPLACE(STR(?current), "^.*[#/]", ""))) AS ?currentLabel)
  OPTIONAL {
    SELECT ?self (GROUP_CONCAT(?pill; separator=" ") AS ?pills) WHERE {
      { SELECT ?self ?pill ?key WHERE {
          ?node c:textOf $this ; c:chosen true ; l10n:label ?pillLabel ; c:searchKey ?key .
          FILTER EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput }
          BIND(CONCAT("‹", STR(?pillLabel), "›") AS ?pill)
          BIND($this AS ?self)
        } ORDER BY ?key }
    } GROUP BY ?self
  }
  BIND(IF(?multi, CONCAT(?caption, ": ", IF(BOUND(?pills), CONCAT(?pills, " "), ""), "[", COALESCE(STR(?typed0), ""), "_]"),
                  CONCAT(?caption, ": [", COALESCE(STR(?typed0), ?currentLabel, ""), "_] ▾")) AS ?lineData)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~root")) AS ?root)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~line")) AS ?line)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~line-text")) AS ?lineText)
}""" .

# --- the options: one component each, minted once ------------------------------------------------------
# It does not hear typing: it watches where options come from, and re-runs when the texts layer's
# nodes change (an option added, relabelled, translated). Each option's rank is its list position
# or sem:order (the least, for an option from two sources) and its search key. Under c:optionLimit
# it is not run: c:TypeaheadMatches mints the best few instead.

c:TypeaheadOptions a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:awaitsWork <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/14> ; # its function twin comes with the combobox work
    sem:targets c:Typeahead ;
    sem:requires c:controls ;
    sem:stratum 0 ;
    sem:readsMinted true ;
    sem:unless c:optionLimit ;
    sem:watches rdf:type , c:controls , c:property , c:options , c:optionClass , c:optionsInUse , c:optionsFrom , c:optionLimit .
c:TypeaheadOptions-sparql a sem:Rule ;
    sem:implements c:TypeaheadOptions ;
    sem:modality mod:Screen ;
    sem:construct """
CONSTRUCT {
  ?list rdfhtml:hasChild ?item .
  ?item a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?opt ; c:label ?label ; c:searchKey ?key ; c:matchKey ?matchKey ; c:detail ?detail ;
        c:rank ?rank ; sem:orderKey ?rank .
}
WHERE {
  $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:Typeahead .
  { SELECT ?self ?opt (MIN(?position) AS ?n) WHERE {
      $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:Typeahead .
      BIND($this AS ?self)
      {
        $this c:options ?head . ?head rdf:rest* ?cell . ?cell rdf:first ?opt .
        { SELECT ?self ?cell (COUNT(?mid) AS ?position) WHERE {
            $this c:options ?head2 . ?head2 rdf:rest* ?mid . ?mid rdf:rest* ?cell .
            BIND($this AS ?self)
          } GROUP BY ?self ?cell }
      } UNION {
        FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:options ?explicit }
        { $this c:optionClass ?class } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:optionClass ?declared } FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:optionsFrom ?lister } $this c:property/rdfs:range ?class }
        ?opt a ?class FILTER(isIRI(?opt))
        OPTIONAL { ?opt sem:order ?order }
        BIND(COALESCE(xsd:integer(ROUND(xsd:decimal(?order))), 0) AS ?position)
      } UNION {
        FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:options ?explicit }
        $this c:optionsInUse ?inUse FILTER(STR(?inUse) = "true")
        $this c:property ?used . ?anyone ?used ?opt .
        BIND(0 AS ?position)
      } UNION {
        FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:options ?explicit }
        $this c:optionsFrom ?source . ?source c:lists ?opt .
        BIND(0 AS ?position)
      }
    } GROUP BY ?self ?opt }
  FILTER(?self = $this)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~term-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?opt)))) AS ?textNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?textNode l10n:label ?localLabel } OPTIONAL { ?textNode c:searchKey ?foldedKey } OPTIONAL { ?textNode c:matchKey ?foldedMatch }
            OPTIONAL { ?textNode c:detail ?detail0 } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?opt rdfs:label ?plain FILTER(isLiteral(?plain) && lang(?plain) = "") } }
  BIND(STR(COALESCE(?localLabel, IF(isLiteral(?opt), STR(?opt), ?plain), REPLACE(STR(?opt), "^.*[#/]", ""))) AS ?label)
  BIND(COALESCE(STR(?foldedKey), LCASE(?label)) AS ?key)
  BIND(COALESCE(STR(?foldedMatch), ?key) AS ?matchKey)
  BIND(STR(?detail0) AS ?detail)
  BIND(xsd:integer(IF(?n < 0, 0, IF(?n > 999999, 999999, ?n))) AS ?clamped)
  BIND(CONCAT(SUBSTR("000000", STRLEN(STR(?clamped)) + 1), STR(?clamped), " ", ?key) AS ?rank)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~list")) AS ?list)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~opt-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?opt)))) AS ?item)
}""" .

# The best matches, under c:optionLimit: while the list is open, the options whose match key
# contains the typed text, best first - the exact name or detail, then those where a name, a word
# of it or the detail starts with the text, then the rest; each the shorter first, then by rank -
# and only as many as the limit. SPARQL's LIMIT is a number in the query, so the rule takes the
# first 50 and counts, for each, the better ones among them (50 is the most it shows). It reads the
# text nodes, which list every option already: a keystroke is one query, a scan of their keys, and
# writes only the rows that came, went or moved. Closed, it lists nothing.

c:TypeaheadMatches a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:awaitsWork <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/14> ; # its function twin comes with the combobox work
    sem:targets c:Typeahead ;
    sem:stratum 0 ;
    sem:readsMinted true ;
    sem:requires c:optionLimit ;
    sem:watches rdf:type , c:optionLimit , c:foldedQuery , c:expanded , c:disabled .
c:TypeaheadMatches-sparql a sem:Rule ;
    sem:implements c:TypeaheadMatches ;
    sem:modality mod:Screen ;
    sem:bulk false ;
    sem:construct """
CONSTRUCT {
  ?list rdfhtml:hasChild ?item .
  ?item a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?opt ; c:label ?label ; c:searchKey ?key ; c:matchKey ?matchKey ; c:detail ?detail ;
        c:rank ?rank ; sem:orderKey ?rank .
}
WHERE {
  $this c:optionLimit ?limit0 .
  BIND(xsd:integer(STR(?limit0)) AS ?limit)
  {
    SELECT ?opt ?rank ((COUNT(?betterRank) - 1) AS ?before) WHERE {
      { SELECT ?opt ?rank WHERE {
          $this c:expanded ?open .
          ?t c:textOf $this ; c:offered true ; c:textFor ?opt ; c:searchKey ?k0 ; c:matchKey ?mk0 ; c:rank ?base .
          FILTER(STR(?open) = "true")
          FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?off FILTER(STR(?off) = "true") }
          FILTER(NOT EXISTS { ?t c:chosen true } || NOT EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput })
          OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?q0 }
          BIND(COALESCE(STR(?q0), "") AS ?q)
          BIND(STR(?k0) AS ?k)
          BIND(STR(?mk0) AS ?mk)
          FILTER(CONTAINS(?mk, ?q))
          BIND(STRAFTER(?mk, "\\n") AS ?dk)
          BIND(IF(?q != "" && (?k = ?q || ?dk = ?q), "0",
                  IF(STRSTARTS(?k, ?q) || STRSTARTS(?dk, ?q) || CONTAINS(?mk, CONCAT(" ", ?q)) || CONTAINS(?mk, CONCAT(":", ?q)) || CONTAINS(?mk, CONCAT("-", ?q)), "1", "2")) AS ?quality)
          BIND(IF(?q = "", 0, IF(STRLEN(?k) > 999, 999, STRLEN(?k))) AS ?n)
          BIND(CONCAT(?quality, SUBSTR("000", STRLEN(STR(?n)) + 1), STR(?n), " ", STR(?base), " ", STR(?opt)) AS ?rank)
        } ORDER BY ?rank LIMIT 50 }
      { SELECT (?rank AS ?betterRank) WHERE {
          $this c:expanded ?open .
          ?t c:textOf $this ; c:offered true ; c:textFor ?opt ; c:searchKey ?k0 ; c:matchKey ?mk0 ; c:rank ?base .
          FILTER(STR(?open) = "true")
          FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?off FILTER(STR(?off) = "true") }
          FILTER(NOT EXISTS { ?t c:chosen true } || NOT EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput })
          OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?q0 }
          BIND(COALESCE(STR(?q0), "") AS ?q)
          BIND(STR(?k0) AS ?k)
          BIND(STR(?mk0) AS ?mk)
          FILTER(CONTAINS(?mk, ?q))
          BIND(STRAFTER(?mk, "\\n") AS ?dk)
          BIND(IF(?q != "" && (?k = ?q || ?dk = ?q), "0",
                  IF(STRSTARTS(?k, ?q) || STRSTARTS(?dk, ?q) || CONTAINS(?mk, CONCAT(" ", ?q)) || CONTAINS(?mk, CONCAT(":", ?q)) || CONTAINS(?mk, CONCAT("-", ?q)), "1", "2")) AS ?quality)
          BIND(IF(?q = "", 0, IF(STRLEN(?k) > 999, 999, STRLEN(?k))) AS ?n)
          BIND(CONCAT(?quality, SUBSTR("000", STRLEN(STR(?n)) + 1), STR(?n), " ", STR(?base), " ", STR(?opt)) AS ?rank)
        } ORDER BY ?rank LIMIT 50 }
      FILTER(?betterRank <= ?rank)
    } GROUP BY ?opt ?rank
  }
  FILTER(?before < ?limit)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~term-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?opt)))) AS ?textNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?textNode l10n:label ?label0 } OPTIONAL { ?textNode c:searchKey ?key0 } OPTIONAL { ?textNode c:matchKey ?matchKey0 }
            OPTIONAL { ?textNode c:detail ?detail0 } }
  BIND(STR(?label0) AS ?label)
  BIND(STR(?key0) AS ?key)
  BIND(STR(?matchKey0) AS ?matchKey)
  BIND(STR(?detail0) AS ?detail)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~list")) AS ?list)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~opt-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?opt)))) AS ?item)
}""" .

# One option. Matching is containment of the folded query in the match key (the folded label, and
# the folded detail after a line break); the key has a character for each of theirs, so the match
# is cut out of the label, or the detail, where it is in the key. Hidden rows stay in the list
# (they do not match now; the next keystroke may show them).

# An option may also say what it does (c:help, a line after its label) and the keys that do the same
# (key:hint: shown in Apple or other glyphs, as the keyboard layer's hints are, and announced with
# aria-keyshortcuts) - a command palette's options do.
c:TypeaheadOptionRendering a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:awaitsWork <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/14> ; # its function twin comes with the combobox work
    sem:targets c:TypeaheadOption ;
    sem:stratum 0 ;
    sem:follows c:of ;
    sem:watches rdf:type , c:of , c:option , c:label , c:searchKey , c:matchKey , c:detail , c:help , key:hint , c:foldedQuery .
c:TypeaheadOptionRendering-fn a sem:Rule ; sem:implements c:TypeaheadOptionRendering ; sem:modality mod:Screen ; sem:function "typeahead:option" .
c:TypeaheadOptionRendering-sparql a sem:Rule ;
    sem:implements c:TypeaheadOptionRendering ;
    sem:modality mod:Screen ;
    sem:construct """
CONSTRUCT {
  ?root a rdfhtml:Li ; sem:renders $this ; rdfhtml:id ?rootId ; rdfhtml:hidden ?hidden ; rdfhtml:attribute ?role, ?shortcuts ;
        rdfhtml:hasChild ?text, ?gap, ?detailEl, ?helpEl, ?keys ; c:optionRow ?typeahead ; c:pick ?opt .
  ?text a rdfhtml:Span ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-label" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?pre, ?hit, ?post ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?afterText .
  ?gap a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data " " ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?detailEl .
  ?detailEl a rdfhtml:Span ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-detail" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?dpre, ?dhit, ?dpost ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?afterDetail .
  ?dpre a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?dpreText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?dafterPre .
  ?dhit a rdfhtml:Mark ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?dhitText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?dpost .
  ?dhitText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?dhitData .
  ?dpost a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?dpostText .
  ?role a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "role" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "option" .
  ?pre a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?preText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?afterPre .
  ?hit a rdfhtml:Mark ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?hitText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?post .
  ?hitText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?hitData .
  ?post a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?postText .
  ?helpEl a rdfhtml:Span ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-help" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?helpText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?keys .
  ?helpText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?help .
  ?keys a rdfhtml:Span ; rdfhtml:class "sem-ta-keys" ; rdfhtml:attribute ?keysHidden ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?apple, ?other .
  ?keysHidden a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-hidden" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue "true" .
  ?apple a rdfhtml:Kbd ; rdfhtml:class "sem-apple" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?appleText ; ord:immediatelyPrecedes ?other .
  ?appleText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?appleValue .
  ?other a rdfhtml:Kbd ; rdfhtml:class "sem-other" ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?otherText .
  ?otherText a rdfhtml:Text ; rdfhtml:data ?otherValue .
  ?shortcuts a rdfhtml:Attribute ; rdfhtml:attributeName "aria-keyshortcuts" ; rdfhtml:attributeValue ?ariaValue .
}
WHERE {
  $this a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of ?typeahead ; c:option ?opt ; c:label ?label0 ; c:searchKey ?key0 .
  BIND(STR(?label0) AS ?label)
  BIND(STR(?key0) AS ?key)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?typeahead c:foldedQuery ?query } }
  BIND(COALESCE(STR(?query), "") AS ?q)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { $this c:matchKey ?matchKey0 } OPTIONAL { $this c:detail ?detail0 } }
  BIND(COALESCE(STR(?matchKey0), ?key) AS ?mk)
  BIND(STR(?detail0) AS ?detail)
  BIND(?q = "" || CONTAINS(?mk, ?q) AS ?matches)
  BIND(IF(?matches, ?none, "") AS ?hidden)
  # Where the match is: in the label (before the line break), or in the detail (after it).
  BIND(IF(?q != "" && ?matches, STRLEN(STRBEFORE(?mk, ?q)), -1) AS ?found)
  BIND(STRLEN(?label) AS ?n)
  BIND(IF(?found >= 0 && ?found < ?n, ?found, -1) AS ?at)
  BIND(IF(?found > ?n, ?found - ?n - 1, -1) AS ?dat)
  BIND(IF(?at >= 0, SUBSTR(?label, 1, ?at), ?label) AS ?pre0)
  BIND(IF(?pre0 != "", ?pre0, ?none) AS ?preText)
  BIND(IF(?at >= 0, SUBSTR(?label, ?at + 1, STRLEN(?q)), ?none) AS ?hitData)
  BIND(IF(?at >= 0, SUBSTR(?label, ?at + 1 + STRLEN(?q)), "") AS ?post0)
  BIND(IF(?post0 != "", ?post0, ?none) AS ?postText)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~root")) AS ?root)
  BIND(STR(?root) AS ?rootId)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~root-role")) AS ?role)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~text")) AS ?text)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?preText), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~pre")), ?none) AS ?pre)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hitData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~hit")), ?none) AS ?hit)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hitData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~hit-text")), ?none) AS ?hitText)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?postText), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~post")), ?none) AS ?post)
  BIND(COALESCE(?hit, ?post) AS ?afterPre)
  # The detail, cut the same way, after a space (so the option's name reads as two words).
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?detail), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~detail")), ?none) AS ?detailEl)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?detail), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~gap")), ?none) AS ?gap)
  BIND(IF(?dat >= 0, SUBSTR(?detail, 1, ?dat), ?detail) AS ?dpre0)
  BIND(IF(?dpre0 != "", ?dpre0, ?none) AS ?dpreText)
  BIND(IF(?dat >= 0, SUBSTR(?detail, ?dat + 1, STRLEN(?q)), ?none) AS ?dhitData)
  BIND(IF(?dat >= 0, SUBSTR(?detail, ?dat + 1 + STRLEN(?q)), "") AS ?dpost0)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?detail) && ?dpost0 != "", ?dpost0, ?none) AS ?dpostText)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?dpreText), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~dpre")), ?none) AS ?dpre)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?dhitData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~dhit")), ?none) AS ?dhit)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?dhitData), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~dhit-text")), ?none) AS ?dhitText)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?dpostText), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~dpost")), ?none) AS ?dpost)
  BIND(COALESCE(?dhit, ?dpost) AS ?dafterPre)
  # What it does, and its keys (normalized and spelled as the keyboard layer's key:Shortcuts-sparql does).
  OPTIONAL { $this c:help ?help0 FILTER(STR(?help0) != "") }
  BIND(STR(?help0) AS ?help)
  OPTIONAL { $this key:hint ?hint0 FILTER(STR(?hint0) != "") }
  VALUES (?pluses ?ends ?modifiers) { ("(\\\\s*\\\\+\\\\s*)+" "^[\\\\s+]+|[\\\\s+]+$" "\\\\+(?:(?:mod|ctrl|alt|shift|meta)\\\\+)+") }
  BIND(CONCAT("+", REPLACE(REPLACE(LCASE(STR(?hint0)), ?pluses, "+"), ?ends, ""), "+") AS ?parts)
  BIND(CONTAINS(?parts, "+mod+") AS ?mod)
  BIND(CONTAINS(?parts, "+ctrl+") AS ?ctrl)
  BIND(CONTAINS(?parts, "+alt+") AS ?alt)
  BIND(CONTAINS(?parts, "+shift+") AS ?shift)
  BIND(CONTAINS(?parts, "+meta+") AS ?meta)
  BIND(REPLACE(?parts, ?modifiers, "+") AS ?keyParts)
  BIND(SUBSTR(?keyParts, 2, STRLEN(?keyParts) - 2) AS ?k0)
  BIND(IF(STRLEN(?k0) = 1, UCASE(?k0), CONCAT(UCASE(SUBSTR(?k0, 1, 1)), SUBSTR(?k0, 2))) AS ?k)
  BIND(CONCAT(IF(?mod, "⌘", ""), IF(?ctrl, "⌃", ""), IF(?alt, "⌥", ""), IF(?shift, "⇧", ""), IF(?meta, "◆", ""), ?k) AS ?appleValue)
  BIND(CONCAT(IF(?mod, "Ctrl+", ""), IF(?ctrl, "Ctrl+", ""), IF(?alt, "Alt+", ""), IF(?shift, "Shift+", ""), IF(?meta, "Win+", ""), ?k) AS ?otherValue)
  BIND(CONCAT(IF(?mod, "Control+", ""), IF(?ctrl, "Control+", ""), IF(?alt, "Alt+", ""), IF(?shift, "Shift+", ""), IF(?meta, "Meta+", ""),
              IF(STRLEN(?k0) = 1, UCASE(?k0), ?k0)) AS ?ariaValue)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?help), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~help")), ?none) AS ?helpEl)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?help), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~help-text")), ?none) AS ?helpText)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hint0), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~keys")), ?none) AS ?keys)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hint0), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~keys-aria-hidden")), ?none) AS ?keysHidden)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hint0), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~apple")), ?none) AS ?apple)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hint0), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~apple-text")), ?none) AS ?appleText)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hint0), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~other")), ?none) AS ?other)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hint0), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~other-text")), ?none) AS ?otherText)
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?hint0), IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~root-aria-keyshortcuts")), ?none) AS ?shortcuts)
  BIND(COALESCE(?helpEl, ?keys) AS ?afterDetail)
  BIND(COALESCE(?gap, ?afterDetail) AS ?afterText)
}""" .

# --- the pills of a tag input --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A c:Tag for each value, small, toned like the value (sty:tone), sorted by its search key, removable
# unless the tag input is disabled. Like the
# options, it re-runs when the texts layer's nodes change (which it does when the values do).

c:TagInputPills a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:awaitsWork <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/14> ; # its function twin comes with the combobox work
    sem:targets c:TagInput ;
    sem:stratum 0 ;
    sem:readsMinted true ;
    sem:watches rdf:type , c:controls , c:property , c:disabled .
c:TagInputPills-sparql a sem:Rule ;
    sem:implements c:TagInputPills ;
    sem:modality mod:Screen ;
    sem:construct """
CONSTRUCT {
  ?pills rdfhtml:hasChild ?item .
  ?item a rdfhtml:Li ; sem:orderKey ?rank ; rdfhtml:hasChild ?tag .
  ?tag a c:Tag ; c:label ?label ; c:removable ?removable ; sty:size sty:Small ; sty:tone ?tone ; c:pillOf $this ; c:tagValue ?value ; c:rank ?rank .
}
WHERE {
  $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput ; c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  ?target ?property ?value .
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~term-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?value)))) AS ?textNode)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?textNode l10n:label ?localLabel } OPTIONAL { ?textNode c:searchKey ?foldedKey } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?value rdfs:label ?plain FILTER(isLiteral(?plain) && lang(?plain) = "") } OPTIONAL { ?value sty:tone ?tone } }
  BIND(STR(COALESCE(?localLabel, IF(isLiteral(?value), STR(?value), ?plain), REPLACE(STR(?value), "^.*[#/]", ""))) AS ?label)
  BIND(CONCAT(COALESCE(STR(?foldedKey), LCASE(?label)), " ", STR(?value)) AS ?rank)
  BIND(IF(EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?disabled FILTER(STR(?disabled) = "true") }, ?none, true) AS ?removable)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~pills")) AS ?pills)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~pill-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?value)))) AS ?item)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR($this), "/~tag-", ENCODE_FOR_URI(STR(?value)))) AS ?tag)
}""" .

# --- behaviour ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key presses the typeaheads react to; other keys are typing (the field handles them). A key a
# reaction used does nothing else (no submit on Enter, no comma typed).

c:TypeaheadKey a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf beh:Event ; beh:domEvent "keydown" ;
    beh:key "arrowdown" , "arrowup" , "enter" , "escape" , "backspace" , "," ;
    rdfs:comment "A key press in a typeahead's field that may move through, pick from or close its list, or add or remove a tag (beh:key)."@en .
c:TypeaheadLeave a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf beh:Event ; beh:domEvent "focusout" ; beh:recorded false ;
    rdfs:comment "The focus left a typeahead's field (to anywhere: its own pills too). Not recorded."@en .

# Typing: the text, the caret, the list opens, nothing is highlighted.
c:TypeaheadInput a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Search the options"@en ;
    beh:when beh:Input ;
    beh:sourceClass c:Typeahead ;
    beh:deletes """CONSTRUCT { $this c:value ?old ; c:caret ?caret ; c:activeOption ?active ; c:error ?error }
WHERE { { $this c:value ?old } UNION { $this c:caret ?caret } UNION { $this c:activeOption ?active } UNION { $this c:error ?error } }""" ;
    beh:inserts """CONSTRUCT { $this c:value ?value ; c:caret ?caret ; c:expanded true }
WHERE { $event beh:value ?value . OPTIONAL { $event beh:caret ?at } BIND(COALESCE(?at, STRLEN(?value)) AS ?caret) }""" .

# A click in the field opens the list; the chevron toggles it (and brings the focus to the field).
c:TypeaheadClick a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Open the list"@en ;
    beh:when beh:Click ;
    beh:sourceClass c:Typeahead ;
    beh:deletes """CONSTRUCT { $this c:expanded ?open ; c:activeOption ?active }
WHERE {
  $event beh:node ?hit FILTER(STR(?hit) = CONCAT(STR($this), "/~chevron"))
  $this c:expanded ?open FILTER(STR(?open) = "true")
  OPTIONAL { $this c:activeOption ?active }
}""" ;
    beh:inserts """CONSTRUCT { $this c:expanded true ; c:caret ?caret }
WHERE {
  $event beh:node ?hit FILTER(STR(?hit) IN (CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input"), CONCAT(STR($this), "/~chevron")))
  $this c:controls ?controlled .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?open FILTER(STR(?open) = "true") }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?disabled FILTER(STR(?disabled) = "true") }
  BIND(IF(STR(?hit) != CONCAT(STR($this), "/~input") && NOT EXISTS { $this c:caret ?at }, 0, ?none) AS ?caret)
}""" .

# Leaving the field closes the list; a combobox gives back its chosen label (the typed text is dropped).
c:TypeaheadClose a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Close the list"@en ;
    beh:when c:TypeaheadLeave ;
    beh:sourceClass c:Typeahead ;
    beh:deletes """CONSTRUCT { $this c:expanded ?open ; c:activeOption ?active ; c:caret ?caret ; c:value ?typed }
WHERE {
  { $this c:expanded ?open } UNION { $this c:activeOption ?active } UNION { $this c:caret ?caret }
  UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } $this c:controls ?controlled ; c:value ?typed }
}""" .

# The arrow keys move through what the list shows: the options that match the typed text (a tag
# input's own values aside), by rank, then the "create" row. They read the option components the
# list is made of (not their rendering, which waits until the list is first shown). Down: the next
# row (wrapping), the first when nothing is highlighted; it opens the list.
c:TypeaheadNext a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Next option"@en ;
    beh:when c:TypeaheadKey ;
    beh:sourceClass c:Typeahead ;
    beh:deletes """
CONSTRUCT { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
WHERE {
  $event beh:key "arrowdown" .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  BIND(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } AS ?multi)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?query } BIND(COALESCE(STR(?query), "") AS ?q)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?o FILTER(STR(?o) = "true") } AS ?open)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
  BIND(IF(?open, COALESCE(?active0, c:Nothing), c:Nothing) AS ?active)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?activeItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?active ; c:rank ?activeRank } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?createRow c:optionRow $this ; c:creates ?entry0 ; c:pick ?createPick } }
  BIND(BOUND(?createPick) && sameTerm(?active, ?createPick) AS ?activeCreates)
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this val:full ?full }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    ?firstItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?firstPick ; c:matchKey ?firstKey ; c:rank ?firstRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?firstKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?firstPick })
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?firstOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?firstOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?firstOtherKey ; c:rank ?firstOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?firstOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?firstOtherPick }) FILTER(?firstOtherRank < ?firstRank) }
  } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(BOUND(?activeRank))
    ?afterItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?afterPick ; c:matchKey ?afterKey ; c:rank ?afterRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?afterKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?afterPick }) FILTER(?afterRank > ?activeRank)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?afterOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?afterOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?afterOtherKey ; c:rank ?afterOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?afterOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?afterOtherPick }) FILTER(?afterOtherRank > ?activeRank) FILTER(?afterOtherRank < ?afterRank) }
  } }
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?activeRank), COALESCE(?afterPick, ?createPick, ?firstPick),
          IF(?activeCreates, COALESCE(?firstPick, ?createPick), COALESCE(?firstPick, ?createPick))) AS ?next)
  FILTER(BOUND(?next))
}""" ;
    beh:inserts """
CONSTRUCT { $this c:activeOption ?next ; c:expanded true }
WHERE {
  $event beh:key "arrowdown" .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  BIND(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } AS ?multi)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?query } BIND(COALESCE(STR(?query), "") AS ?q)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?o FILTER(STR(?o) = "true") } AS ?open)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
  BIND(IF(?open, COALESCE(?active0, c:Nothing), c:Nothing) AS ?active)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?activeItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?active ; c:rank ?activeRank } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?createRow c:optionRow $this ; c:creates ?entry0 ; c:pick ?createPick } }
  BIND(BOUND(?createPick) && sameTerm(?active, ?createPick) AS ?activeCreates)
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this val:full ?full }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    ?firstItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?firstPick ; c:matchKey ?firstKey ; c:rank ?firstRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?firstKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?firstPick })
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?firstOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?firstOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?firstOtherKey ; c:rank ?firstOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?firstOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?firstOtherPick }) FILTER(?firstOtherRank < ?firstRank) }
  } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(BOUND(?activeRank))
    ?afterItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?afterPick ; c:matchKey ?afterKey ; c:rank ?afterRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?afterKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?afterPick }) FILTER(?afterRank > ?activeRank)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?afterOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?afterOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?afterOtherKey ; c:rank ?afterOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?afterOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?afterOtherPick }) FILTER(?afterOtherRank > ?activeRank) FILTER(?afterOtherRank < ?afterRank) }
  } }
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?activeRank), COALESCE(?afterPick, ?createPick, ?firstPick),
          IF(?activeCreates, COALESCE(?firstPick, ?createPick), COALESCE(?firstPick, ?createPick))) AS ?next)
}""" .

# Up: the previous row (wrapping), the last when nothing is highlighted.
c:TypeaheadPrevious a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Previous option"@en ;
    beh:when c:TypeaheadKey ;
    beh:sourceClass c:Typeahead ;
    beh:deletes """
CONSTRUCT { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
WHERE {
  $event beh:key "arrowup" .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  BIND(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } AS ?multi)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?query } BIND(COALESCE(STR(?query), "") AS ?q)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?o FILTER(STR(?o) = "true") } AS ?open)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
  BIND(IF(?open, COALESCE(?active0, c:Nothing), c:Nothing) AS ?active)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?activeItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?active ; c:rank ?activeRank } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?createRow c:optionRow $this ; c:creates ?entry0 ; c:pick ?createPick } }
  BIND(BOUND(?createPick) && sameTerm(?active, ?createPick) AS ?activeCreates)
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this val:full ?full }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    ?lastItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?lastPick ; c:matchKey ?lastKey ; c:rank ?lastRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?lastKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?lastPick })
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?lastOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?lastOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?lastOtherKey ; c:rank ?lastOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?lastOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?lastOtherPick }) FILTER(?lastOtherRank > ?lastRank) }
  } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(BOUND(?activeRank))
    ?beforeItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?beforePick ; c:matchKey ?beforeKey ; c:rank ?beforeRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?beforeKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?beforePick }) FILTER(?beforeRank < ?activeRank)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?beforeOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?beforeOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?beforeOtherKey ; c:rank ?beforeOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?beforeOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?beforeOtherPick }) FILTER(?beforeOtherRank < ?activeRank) FILTER(?beforeOtherRank > ?beforeRank) }
  } }
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?activeRank), COALESCE(?beforePick, ?createPick, ?lastPick),
          IF(?activeCreates, COALESCE(?lastPick, ?createPick), COALESCE(?createPick, ?lastPick))) AS ?next)
  FILTER(BOUND(?next))
}""" ;
    beh:inserts """
CONSTRUCT { $this c:activeOption ?next ; c:expanded true }
WHERE {
  $event beh:key "arrowup" .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  BIND(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } AS ?multi)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?query } BIND(COALESCE(STR(?query), "") AS ?q)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?o FILTER(STR(?o) = "true") } AS ?open)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
  BIND(IF(?open, COALESCE(?active0, c:Nothing), c:Nothing) AS ?active)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?activeItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?active ; c:rank ?activeRank } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?createRow c:optionRow $this ; c:creates ?entry0 ; c:pick ?createPick } }
  BIND(BOUND(?createPick) && sameTerm(?active, ?createPick) AS ?activeCreates)
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this val:full ?full }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    ?lastItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?lastPick ; c:matchKey ?lastKey ; c:rank ?lastRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?lastKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?lastPick })
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?lastOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?lastOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?lastOtherKey ; c:rank ?lastOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?lastOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?lastOtherPick }) FILTER(?lastOtherRank > ?lastRank) }
  } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(BOUND(?activeRank))
    ?beforeItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?beforePick ; c:matchKey ?beforeKey ; c:rank ?beforeRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?beforeKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?beforePick }) FILTER(?beforeRank < ?activeRank)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?beforeOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?beforeOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?beforeOtherKey ; c:rank ?beforeOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?beforeOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?beforeOtherPick }) FILTER(?beforeOtherRank < ?activeRank) FILTER(?beforeOtherRank > ?beforeRank) }
  } }
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?activeRank), COALESCE(?beforePick, ?createPick, ?lastPick),
          IF(?activeCreates, COALESCE(?lastPick, ?createPick), COALESCE(?createPick, ?lastPick))) AS ?next)
}""" .

# Escape: an open list closes, the field showing the typed text again; a closed one clears it.
c:TypeaheadEscape a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Close the list"@en ;
    beh:when c:TypeaheadKey ;
    beh:sourceClass c:Typeahead ;
    beh:deletes """CONSTRUCT { $this c:expanded ?open ; c:activeOption ?active ; c:value ?typed }
WHERE {
  $event beh:key "escape" .
  { $this c:expanded ?open FILTER(STR(?open) = "true") }
  UNION { $this c:activeOption ?active FILTER EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?o1 FILTER(STR(?o1) = "true") } }
  UNION { $this c:value ?typed FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?o2 FILTER(STR(?o2) = "true") } }
}""" .

# Enter (and, in a tag input, a comma) commits: the highlighted row; else the option the text names
# exactly; else the "create" row; else the only option shown; else, with c:picksFirstMatch, the
# first one shown. A combobox replaces its value; a tag input adds one, never one it
# has, nor past its shape's sh:maxCount (val:full). A new resource is typed and labelled. The text
# is cleared and the list closed; the field keeps the focus.
c:TypeaheadCommit a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Pick the option"@en ;
    beh:when c:TypeaheadKey ;
    beh:sourceClass c:Typeahead ;
    beh:deletes """
CONSTRUCT { ?target ?property ?replaced . $this c:value ?typed ; c:activeOption ?active0 ; c:expanded ?open0 ; c:caret ?caret }
WHERE {
  $event beh:key ?key FILTER(?key = "enter" || (?key = "," && EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput }))
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  BIND(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } AS ?multi)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?query } BIND(COALESCE(STR(?query), "") AS ?q)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?o FILTER(STR(?o) = "true") } AS ?open)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
  BIND(IF(?open, COALESCE(?active0, c:Nothing), c:Nothing) AS ?active)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?activeItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?active ; c:rank ?activeRank } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?createRow c:optionRow $this ; c:creates ?entry0 ; c:pick ?createPick } }
  BIND(BOUND(?createPick) && sameTerm(?active, ?createPick) AS ?activeCreates)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(?q != "")
    ?exactItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?exactPick ; c:searchKey ?exactKey ; c:rank ?exactRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?exactKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?exactPick }) FILTER(STR(?exactKey) = ?q)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?exactOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?exactOtherPick ; c:searchKey ?exactOtherKey ; c:rank ?exactOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?exactOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?exactOtherPick }) FILTER(STR(?exactOtherKey) = ?q) FILTER(?exactOtherRank < ?exactRank) }
  } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(?q != "")
    ?onlyItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?onlyPick ; c:matchKey ?onlyKey .
    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?onlyKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?onlyPick })
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?onlyOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?onlyOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?onlyOtherKey . FILTER(?onlyOther != ?onlyItem) FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?onlyOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?onlyOtherPick }) }
  } }
  # With c:picksFirstMatch, the best match shown (the least rank).
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(?q != "" && EXISTS { $this c:picksFirstMatch ?firstMatch FILTER(STR(?firstMatch) = "true") })
    ?bestItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?bestPick ; c:matchKey ?bestKey ; c:rank ?bestRank .
    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?bestKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?bestPick })
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?bestOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?bestOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?bestOtherKey ; c:rank ?bestOtherRank . FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?bestOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?bestOtherPick }) FILTER(?bestOtherRank < ?bestRank) }
  } }
  BIND(IF(?key = "enter" && (BOUND(?activeRank) || ?activeCreates), ?active, COALESCE(?exactPick, ?createPick, ?onlyPick, ?bestPick)) AS ?value)
  FILTER(BOUND(?value))
  FILTER(!?multi || (NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?value } && NOT EXISTS { $this val:full ?full }))
  {
    { FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property . ?target ?property ?replaced }
    UNION { $this c:value ?typed } UNION { $this c:expanded ?open0 } UNION { $this c:caret ?caret }
  }
}""" ;
    beh:inserts """
CONSTRUCT { ?target ?property ?value . ?minted a ?class ; rdfs:label ?entry . $this c:caret 0 }
WHERE {
  $event beh:key ?key FILTER(?key = "enter" || (?key = "," && EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput }))
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  BIND(EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } AS ?multi)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:foldedQuery ?query } BIND(COALESCE(STR(?query), "") AS ?q)
  BIND(EXISTS { $this c:expanded ?o FILTER(STR(?o) = "true") } AS ?open)
  OPTIONAL { $this c:activeOption ?active0 }
  BIND(IF(?open, COALESCE(?active0, c:Nothing), c:Nothing) AS ?active)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?activeItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?active ; c:rank ?activeRank } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?createRow c:optionRow $this ; c:creates ?entry0 ; c:pick ?createPick } }
  BIND(BOUND(?createPick) && sameTerm(?active, ?createPick) AS ?activeCreates)
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(?q != "")
    ?exactItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?exactPick ; c:searchKey ?exactKey ; c:rank ?exactRank .
    FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?exactKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?exactPick }) FILTER(STR(?exactKey) = ?q)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?exactOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?exactOtherPick ; c:searchKey ?exactOtherKey ; c:rank ?exactOtherRank . FILTER(?q = "" || CONTAINS(STR(?exactOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?exactOtherPick }) FILTER(STR(?exactOtherKey) = ?q) FILTER(?exactOtherRank < ?exactRank) }
  } }
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(?q != "")
    ?onlyItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?onlyPick ; c:matchKey ?onlyKey .
    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?onlyKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?onlyPick })
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?onlyOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?onlyOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?onlyOtherKey . FILTER(?onlyOther != ?onlyItem) FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?onlyOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?onlyOtherPick }) }
  } }
  # With c:picksFirstMatch, the best match shown (the least rank).
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL {
    FILTER(?q != "" && EXISTS { $this c:picksFirstMatch ?firstMatch FILTER(STR(?firstMatch) = "true") })
    ?bestItem a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?bestPick ; c:matchKey ?bestKey ; c:rank ?bestRank .
    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?bestKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?bestPick })
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?bestOther a c:TypeaheadOption ; c:of $this ; c:option ?bestOtherPick ; c:matchKey ?bestOtherKey ; c:rank ?bestOtherRank . FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?bestOtherKey), ?q)) FILTER(!?multi || NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?bestOtherPick }) FILTER(?bestOtherRank < ?bestRank) }
  } }
  BIND(IF(?key = "enter" && (BOUND(?activeRank) || ?activeCreates), ?active, COALESCE(?exactPick, ?createPick, ?onlyPick, ?bestPick)) AS ?value)
  FILTER(BOUND(?value))
  FILTER(!?multi || (NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?value } && NOT EXISTS { $this val:full ?full }))
  # A new resource (the create row's c:mints, when it is what is committed) is typed and labelled.
  LATERAL { OPTIONAL { ?createRow c:optionRow $this ; c:mints ?value . BIND(?value AS ?minted) OPTIONAL { ?createRow c:mintClass ?class } } }
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?minted), ?entry0, ?none) AS ?entry)
}""" .

# Clicking a row commits it, as Enter does.
c:TypeaheadPick a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Pick the option"@en ;
    beh:when beh:Click ;
    beh:sourceClass c:Typeahead ;
    beh:deletes """
CONSTRUCT { ?target ?property ?replaced . $this c:value ?typed ; c:activeOption ?active ; c:expanded ?open ; c:caret ?caret }
WHERE {
  $event beh:node ?hit . ?row rdfhtml:hasChild* ?hit . ?row c:optionRow $this ; c:pick ?value .
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  FILTER(NOT EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } || (NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?value } && NOT EXISTS { $this val:full ?full }))
  {
    { FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property . ?target ?property ?replaced }
    UNION { $this c:value ?typed } UNION { $this c:activeOption ?active } UNION { $this c:expanded ?open } UNION { $this c:caret ?caret }
  }
}""" ;
    beh:inserts """
CONSTRUCT { ?target ?property ?value . ?minted a ?class ; rdfs:label ?entry . $this c:caret 0 }
WHERE {
  $event beh:node ?hit . ?row rdfhtml:hasChild* ?hit . ?row c:optionRow $this ; c:pick ?value .
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  FILTER(NOT EXISTS { $this a/rdfs:subClassOf* c:TagInput } || (NOT EXISTS { ?target ?property ?value } && NOT EXISTS { $this val:full ?full }))
  OPTIONAL { ?row c:mints ?minted ; c:creates ?entry . OPTIONAL { ?row c:mintClass ?class } }
}""" .

# A pill's ✕ removes its value (and gives the focus back to the field).
c:TagInputRemove a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Remove the tag"@en ;
    beh:when beh:Click ;
    beh:sourceClass c:TagInput ;
    beh:deletes """
CONSTRUCT { ?target ?property ?value . $this c:caret ?caret }
WHERE {
  $event beh:node ?hit . ?n rdfhtml:hasChild* ?hit . ?n c:removes ?tag . ?tag c:pillOf $this ; c:tagValue ?value .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  OPTIONAL { $this c:caret ?caret }
}""" ;
    beh:inserts """
CONSTRUCT { $this c:caret 0 }
WHERE {
  $event beh:node ?hit . ?n rdfhtml:hasChild* ?hit . ?n c:removes ?tag . ?tag c:pillOf $this .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
}""" .

# Backspace in the empty field removes the last pill.
c:TagInputBackspace a beh:Reaction ;
    rdfs:label "Remove the last tag"@en ;
    beh:when c:TypeaheadKey ;
    beh:sourceClass c:TagInput ;
    beh:deletes """
CONSTRUCT { ?target ?property ?value }
WHERE {
  $event beh:key "backspace" ; beh:value ?typed FILTER(STR(?typed) = "")
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this c:disabled ?d FILTER(STR(?d) = "true") }
  $this c:controls ?target ; c:property ?property .
  ?tag c:pillOf $this ; c:tagValue ?value ; c:rank ?rank .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?other c:pillOf $this ; c:rank ?otherRank FILTER(?otherRank > ?rank) }
}""" .
